# Add exact per-repository exceptions here for trusted upstream URLs that are
# known to fail automated validation. Keep entries narrow and documented.
#
# Example:
# https://cmsweb.cern.ch/das/

# Page loads, but Docker restructured their install docs and the "#server"
# fragment no longer exists upstream. URL is unchanged from the legacy lesson.
https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/#server

# CERN EOS public host does not resolve from outside CERN, so GitHub runners
# cannot reach it either. URL is unchanged from the legacy lesson.
https://eospublichttp.cern.ch//eos/opendata/cms/upload/apb2023/histograms.root

# CITATION.cff only exists in this fork until it is merged upstream, so the
# footer's citation link to hsf-training/hsf-training-docker 404s until then.
https://github.com/hsf-training/hsf-training-docker/blob/gh-pages/CITATION.cff
